        </div>

        <div class="policy-card">
            <h4>1. What Cookies Are</h4>
            <p>Cookies are small text files stored on your device that help websites remember preferences and improve
                your browsing experience.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="policy-card">
            <h4>2. Why We Use Cookies</h4>
            <p>We use cookies to support core site functionality, remember session-level preferences, and improve site
                usability and performance.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="policy-card">
            <h4>3. Analytics and Improvement</h4>
            <p>Some cookies help us understand how pages are used so we can improve navigation, registration flow, and
                content clarity for parents and visitors.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="policy-card">
            <h4>4. Managing Cookies</h4>
            <p>You can manage or disable cookies through your browser settings. Disabling some cookies may impact site
                features and user experience.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="policy-card">
            <h4>5. Third-Party Services</h4>
            <p>Where third-party tools are used (for example payment or infrastructure services), their cookie
                behavior may be governed by their own policies.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="policy-card">
            <h4>6. Policy Updates</h4>
            <p>We may update this Cookies Policy as our services evolve. Please review this page periodically for the
                latest version.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
